cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: 'chess_MHSUC: Human Chess Under Clock Constraints'
abstract: An observational replication and benchmark study of human chess under clock constraints. Saved dense move-quality analyses cover 145,020 games and 8,353,475 filtered move observations across 3+0, 5+0, and 10+0 samples from September and October 2024. A separate 10+0 checkpoint outcome-model comparison finds that the predictive gain from clock features is concentrated in games ending on time. The monthly archive-prefix samples share players; results are predictive and descriptive, not causal.
